  "summary": "A marketplace where providers set their own prices per machine. Each figure is a floor - the median of the five cheapest asks on machines Lium does not mark as reclaimable (its \"secure\" tier) whose provider scores 95 or more on Lium's own 14-day reliability score - withheld when too few are free. The score is Lium's; the 95 threshold is ours. Lium lists only machines free right now, so most cards read \"thin market\" most hours. Machines rented whole are a separate row; its spot machines are not read.",
  "notes": "marketplace, keyless public nodes feed (/api/public/v1/nodes, lists only nodes rentable now); trimmed floor of the 5 cheapest verified asks, withheld when the window cannot carry a floor (fewer than 3, or a median over 3x the cheapest); verified = tier secure and reliability_score >= 95 (Lium's 14-day score, owner's rule of 2026-10-17); single-GPU book = nodes taking an order of one GPU, at price_per_gpu_hour; multi-GPU book = nodes of 2+ GPUs taking no order below two, wholly free, at price_per_node_hour; spot tier not read; links the card page named in /pricing.json",
